WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:09.069 --> 01:12.280
The Bu family owns
six out of ten boats in Dodong-ri.

01:13.198 --> 01:15.992
Eight out of ten people in this town
work with them.

01:16.076 --> 01:17.243
Gwan-sik is screwed.

01:19.287 --> 01:21.748
It's not just Sang-gil. It's all of them.

01:22.332 --> 01:25.210
His brother is village chief
and an even bigger asshat.

01:26.294 --> 01:27.879
You know how island people get.

01:28.379 --> 01:29.756
Bunch of little tyrants.

01:31.007 --> 01:32.008
Ah.

01:35.220 --> 01:36.387
What happened?

01:37.138 --> 01:38.515
He wouldn't hire you again?

01:39.557 --> 01:40.767
He blamed the economy.

01:40.850 --> 01:43.853
As if the economy
ever stopped anyone from fishing.

01:43.937 --> 01:45.105
Just go home!

01:45.772 --> 01:46.773
Hey.

01:49.484 --> 01:52.278
I hear they're building a road
around Hallasan Mountain.

01:52.362 --> 01:53.947
Tell him to find a job there.

01:54.030 --> 01:56.533
Whether it's in the field or in a boat,
a paycheck's a paycheck.

01:58.827 --> 02:01.204
Conches for sale!
Top quality! Haenyeocaught!

02:01.287 --> 02:04.541
We have conches, extra-fresh.
Meongge as well!

02:06.126 --> 02:08.795
Poor boy. He's always the first
to arrive every morning.

02:08.878 --> 02:11.256
He says it's his only chance
to get a spot on a boat.

02:11.881 --> 02:15.426
Gwan-sik has to be first to even
get a chance to be considered for it.

02:16.302 --> 02:17.554
It's not fair.

02:18.054 --> 02:19.973
He has it a lot harder than the others.

02:20.473 --> 02:22.433
What about working on land?

02:22.517 --> 02:23.935
How does that sit with him?

02:25.645 --> 02:28.064
He doesn't talk much. He's a quiet guy.

02:28.148 --> 02:30.150
No wonder he doesn't like it.

02:30.650 --> 02:33.236
A man of the sea
will always yearn for the sea.

02:39.826 --> 02:40.827
Good Lord.

02:41.494 --> 02:43.705
What is it this time?

02:44.205 --> 02:46.291
What have they done to your arm?

02:47.667 --> 02:50.336
I just don't have the skill set,
I guess, so…

02:51.671 --> 02:53.423
Did they tell you not to come back?

02:55.091 --> 02:56.509
Poor boy.

02:59.220 --> 03:02.390
Why did he bother to fix
a perfectly good roof?

03:13.026 --> 03:14.819
He should've just taken a break.

03:16.362 --> 03:18.072
He was wilting away.

03:22.243 --> 03:26.039
What else could happen to
a hard-working man who couldn't find work?

03:28.833 --> 03:31.461
He made all these already?

03:31.961 --> 03:34.297
We had three days to work on them.

03:37.091 --> 03:38.301
Mom once said

03:39.219 --> 03:41.638
that the leftover cabbages in the field

03:41.721 --> 03:44.432
looked less wilted
than Dad lying on his side.

03:47.644 --> 03:50.647
DODONG-RI VARIETY SHOP

04:14.587 --> 04:16.881
Lie down. I've already started the rice.

04:20.260 --> 04:21.761
Go easy on yourself.

04:22.345 --> 04:23.596
Take it slow.

04:26.307 --> 04:27.892
You're not a plow ox.

04:29.018 --> 04:30.895
You've been selling fish
since you were nine,

04:30.979 --> 04:32.981
and you're allowed to rest for once.

04:34.607 --> 04:36.567
Think of this as a vacation.

04:38.111 --> 04:39.195
I've never had one.

04:41.489 --> 04:42.782
It feels strange.

04:44.534 --> 04:45.368
Very strange.

04:47.203 --> 04:49.580
Hey, you deserve a break more than anyone.

04:49.664 --> 04:51.874
There's no law against
enjoying yourself, is there?

04:52.458 --> 04:53.418
If I do that,

04:54.127 --> 04:55.753
our family of four will starve.

04:59.465 --> 05:00.466
It's simple.

05:01.342 --> 05:03.886
If I work for one day,
we can live for one day.

05:05.972 --> 05:07.140
I just wish finding it…

05:09.642 --> 05:10.601
was that simple.

05:15.606 --> 05:17.525
Why worry about starving?

05:18.943 --> 05:21.988
I'll earn the money if we are short.

05:26.784 --> 05:28.244
Coming from the bookworm

05:29.245 --> 05:31.456
who couldn't sell a cabbage
to save her life?

05:49.390 --> 05:51.684
Standing before the empty rice jar,

05:52.268 --> 05:56.439
Mom remembered the smile she saw
so often on her own mother's face.

06:00.360 --> 06:03.863
She remembered how her mother
forced herself to wear that smile

06:03.946 --> 06:06.449
if it meant she could sell another conch.

06:07.825 --> 06:10.286
Excuse me, uh,

06:10.870 --> 06:12.372
we're out of rice.

06:13.414 --> 06:14.248
Could I borrow--

06:14.332 --> 06:16.876
I don't understand
what you're saying, girl.

06:18.586 --> 06:20.463
What are you complaining about?

06:20.963 --> 06:22.548
There's plenty of folks worse off.

06:29.514 --> 06:32.058
It must have looked
exactly like the smile I remember

06:32.141 --> 06:33.434
on Mom's young face.

06:33.518 --> 06:36.020
It must have been forced just the same.

06:38.898 --> 06:41.692
I swear, those ladies
always rip off your dad.

06:41.776 --> 06:43.820
They charge a thousand won more.

06:43.903 --> 06:47.615
Wow, haggling over 1,000 won?
You really are a mom.

06:50.743 --> 06:51.577
What?

06:52.286 --> 06:53.538
It's funny, is all.

06:54.288 --> 06:55.498
When I was younger,

06:55.581 --> 06:58.126
I couldn't even sell a cabbage
to save my life.

06:58.626 --> 06:59.961
Seriously?

07:00.044 --> 07:02.213
I was such
a shy little bookworm back then.

07:03.589 --> 07:06.509
Whenever I sold cabbages
in my school uniform,

07:06.592 --> 07:08.928
I held my book up this close to my face.

07:09.011 --> 07:11.013
I was so embarrassed.

07:11.097 --> 07:13.224
You were cool.
What happened?

07:14.851 --> 07:16.978
I learned what things in life

07:17.061 --> 07:19.230
are actually worth being ashamed of.

07:20.815 --> 07:23.359
For example,
the sound of three growling stomachs

07:23.443 --> 07:25.153
of your family in the night.

07:26.154 --> 07:28.698
It's the sound of them going hungry.

07:30.366 --> 07:32.785
There's nothing more embarrassing
than that.

07:35.997 --> 07:39.083
Back then, I was so inexperienced.

07:40.126 --> 07:43.546
For some reason,
it all felt so humiliating and pathetic.

07:45.298 --> 07:48.217
There were many times
when I wanted to give up on life.

07:48.926 --> 07:50.470
Say something already.

07:50.553 --> 07:52.763
Nothing will get fixed
if you just sit there.

07:53.598 --> 07:54.640
You wanna borrow our money?

07:54.724 --> 07:56.392
What's the use
of trying to keep your pride?

07:56.476 --> 07:59.312
If you can't say anything,
why bother coming here at all?

08:01.856 --> 08:04.275
Well? What have you come for, kid?

08:05.276 --> 08:07.653
Ae-sun, you don't live here anymore.

08:07.737 --> 08:08.988
You live with them.

08:09.489 --> 08:11.574
You should be asking his family for help.

08:11.657 --> 08:13.868
Why come here
with that long face of yours?

08:15.328 --> 08:17.413
I thought you could
care for yourself like your mother,

08:17.497 --> 08:19.165
but you're as hopeless as your father.

08:19.749 --> 08:20.833
You can't make ends meet?

08:21.751 --> 08:24.837
And what if she can't?
We don't have any land left to sell.

08:27.256 --> 08:31.135
You must really be desperate to come here,
but we're buried in debt ourselves.

08:39.894 --> 08:42.230
Marriage was supposed to
make your life better.

08:43.814 --> 08:45.733
Okay, fine, just give her the ring.

08:47.068 --> 08:47.902
Damn it.

08:52.281 --> 08:53.157
Oh my.

08:54.867 --> 08:57.078
You don't have food to feed your child,

08:57.161 --> 08:58.955
and you're too proud to beg?

09:04.252 --> 09:06.295
You are still a little girl.

09:16.889 --> 09:17.723
Honey.

09:18.975 --> 09:19.809
Hmm?

09:21.686 --> 09:22.979
All I want

09:24.772 --> 09:27.233
is to get old as fast as I can.

09:30.444 --> 09:31.279
Why?

09:31.821 --> 09:32.738
Because

09:34.407 --> 09:37.243
I always assumed when I was a grown-up,

09:37.994 --> 09:41.414
I'd know how to manage problems
and tough issues.

09:42.832 --> 09:44.458
Just like Auntie Gyeong-ja.

09:45.001 --> 09:47.295
Even if creditors invaded the house,

09:48.337 --> 09:50.464
I thought every adult would be fine.

09:54.802 --> 09:56.679
I thought that when you grow up…

09:58.931 --> 10:02.393
you would grow callouses
on your heart to withstand fire.

10:06.355 --> 10:08.399
Here we are still getting burned.

10:11.027 --> 10:12.612
It just burns us,

10:13.529 --> 10:14.739
and it always hurts.

10:16.741 --> 10:18.284
I can't be the only one.

10:18.784 --> 10:20.244
Is everyone else

10:20.745 --> 10:22.663
growing up just fine, you think?

10:24.624 --> 10:25.958
I think they're all

10:27.418 --> 10:29.754
just pretending.

10:30.630 --> 10:32.173
That's all a grown-up is.

10:36.844 --> 10:39.555
Then I just wish it would happen faster.

10:43.059 --> 10:44.685
Because it's too much.

10:45.895 --> 10:48.522
Learning to be a mom, a wife,

10:48.606 --> 10:50.441
and an adult all at once.

10:51.192 --> 10:53.110
I just don't understand…

10:55.613 --> 10:57.657
why everything has to be so hard.

11:19.011 --> 11:19.887
Hold me.

11:25.851 --> 11:26.977
Pat my back.

11:38.447 --> 11:43.452
♪ Hush, little baby
Don't say a word ♪

11:44.120 --> 11:49.125
♪ Mama's gonna buy you a mockingbird ♪

11:50.000 --> 11:54.922
♪ And if that mockingbird don't sing ♪

11:56.590 --> 12:01.429
♪ Mama's gonna buy you a diamond ring ♪

12:01.929 --> 12:05.850
♪ And if that diamond ring is brass ♪

12:05.933 --> 12:06.809
Ae-sun.

12:09.729 --> 12:10.730
Wake up, dear.

12:20.865 --> 12:23.951
Were you losing sleep
because you didn't give me the ring?

12:33.043 --> 12:35.337
Careful. Watch your leg, all right?

12:35.421 --> 12:36.881
My husband's right there.

12:39.592 --> 12:41.051
Hey, don't take that out.

12:41.135 --> 12:44.388
If you gave us your savings,
I'd never forgive myself.

12:45.556 --> 12:46.891
Buy a boat.

12:46.974 --> 12:48.184
I'm sorry?

12:48.267 --> 12:50.269
Buy a boat,
and don't say a word.

12:50.936 --> 12:53.856
If they ask where you got the money,
say you won the lottery.

13:01.947 --> 13:04.074
-Did… did you steal this?
-It's mine.

13:04.158 --> 13:07.912
It's the money from my gukbap stand
before the war.

13:09.580 --> 13:11.582
You've kept it this entire time?

13:11.665 --> 13:15.127
My grandson would have gambled it
all away long ago if I hadn't.

13:16.837 --> 13:18.756
So you hid it to give it to me?

13:18.839 --> 13:20.382
Your mother made me promise.

13:21.592 --> 13:23.010
She said this would make us even.

13:23.719 --> 13:24.553
Huh?

13:28.015 --> 13:29.809
She has to live. She has to.

13:29.892 --> 13:32.603
What will happen to
her poor little children?

13:35.314 --> 13:36.315
Mother.

13:40.402 --> 13:41.403
Mother.

13:48.536 --> 13:50.454
Mother, can we go somewhere together?

13:51.914 --> 13:53.249
I'm a little scared.

13:53.749 --> 13:55.543
FOREVER YOUNG STUDIO

14:01.215 --> 14:03.843
Didn't I buy this for you
when you got married?

14:06.303 --> 14:09.765
You know, this outfit
is still the best one I have.

14:13.644 --> 14:16.105
I guess it's because of
the dangers of the job.

14:17.940 --> 14:20.442
But we haenyeos are very superstitious.

14:21.068 --> 14:22.987
We believe when we take a photo,

14:23.070 --> 14:25.364
that photo will be used for our funeral.

14:27.324 --> 14:30.619
To think that
I risk my life just for work,

14:31.579 --> 14:33.080
but I still fear death.

14:34.081 --> 14:35.708
I'm afraid to take this picture.

14:35.791 --> 14:37.084
Look at me, dear.

14:48.721 --> 14:51.682
This photo is what
your children will remember you by.

14:52.850 --> 14:54.977
So put on some pink lipstick.

14:58.397 --> 14:59.815
Let's take one for you,

15:00.733 --> 15:02.401
then I'll take one too.

15:05.112 --> 15:07.031
You need to stay alive.

15:07.114 --> 15:08.991
There's plenty of time to join me.

15:14.496 --> 15:16.457
I've outlived my child

15:17.791 --> 15:19.543
for far too long now.

15:20.669 --> 15:22.588
Even after I lost my son,

15:22.671 --> 15:24.423
I still find myself here,

15:24.506 --> 15:27.009
eating three square meals a day.

15:32.181 --> 15:33.390
I promise you

15:34.350 --> 15:36.143
I'll find your precious son.

15:39.188 --> 15:41.565
I'll stay by his side in the afterlife.

15:42.566 --> 15:44.318
I won't look for a new guy.

15:47.029 --> 15:49.073
If you see Han-gyu before I do,

15:50.908 --> 15:52.493
just tell him I'm sorry.

15:55.329 --> 15:57.498
Tell him his mom is so sorry.

15:58.082 --> 16:00.417
Please tell him so.

16:01.543 --> 16:02.628
Please tell him.

16:11.178 --> 16:13.764
I'll make sure
he hears that loud and clear.

16:15.015 --> 16:16.225
But in the meantime,

16:17.142 --> 16:18.936
Han-gyu's daughter needs you.

16:20.562 --> 16:22.272
Watch over Ae-sun like

16:23.023 --> 16:24.775
you'd watch over Han-gyu.

16:29.029 --> 16:29.905
I see.

16:32.116 --> 16:34.159
So that's why you have brought me here.

16:34.827 --> 16:36.954
You couldn't leave that child on her own.

16:39.915 --> 16:41.458
She'll become an orphan,

16:42.835 --> 16:44.586
and she's only ten years old.

16:45.796 --> 16:48.132
She needs someone
to rely on in this world.

16:52.219 --> 16:53.887
Me and my misfortune.

16:53.971 --> 16:56.473
First, I lost my son, and now you.

16:57.725 --> 16:59.518
She is thoughtful, and

17:00.519 --> 17:02.146
she won't be a bother to you.

17:03.188 --> 17:04.898
But if the day comes
when she seeks you out,

17:05.482 --> 17:08.694
after trying her best
to… to stand on her own feet,

17:10.904 --> 17:13.115
it's because
life has been unbearably hard.

17:15.659 --> 17:17.369
I'm asking you to help her.

17:21.749 --> 17:23.417
That girl can withstand

17:24.710 --> 17:25.961
any kind of storm.

17:29.590 --> 17:30.966
But if she says…

17:32.968 --> 17:34.845
"…Please, Grandma, I need some help,"

17:35.471 --> 17:36.805
then you give it to her

17:38.223 --> 17:40.142
as you would have given it to Han-gyu.

17:42.186 --> 17:44.396
That's all I ask. Just one time.

17:45.647 --> 17:47.066
Help her that one time.

17:49.443 --> 17:51.445
You wouldn't owe Han-gyu a thing,

17:51.528 --> 17:54.156
and there'd be nothing
for you to be sorry for.

17:54.239 --> 17:56.241
Oh, sweetheart.

17:56.825 --> 17:58.368
I'll always be her grandma.

17:58.452 --> 18:02.081
But you have so little time left.
Why waste it on me?

18:03.499 --> 18:05.209
I can't die just yet.

18:06.460 --> 18:08.212
I can't go yet.

18:09.296 --> 18:10.297
My dear.

18:13.717 --> 18:15.010
You go in peace.

18:16.261 --> 18:17.805
Go in peace.

18:43.956 --> 18:47.376
Here we go.
One, two, three.

19:04.434 --> 19:05.269
Grandma?

19:07.646 --> 19:10.649
When I'm a grandma,
will I miss her any less, you think?

19:12.943 --> 19:14.653
No, my child. You won't.

19:17.030 --> 19:18.991
The longer you live,
the more you understand

19:19.074 --> 19:22.870
what your parents went through
to keep their children in their hearts.

19:24.079 --> 19:25.080
When your parents die,

19:26.290 --> 19:28.458
you let them go into the afterlife,

19:29.042 --> 19:30.794
but when your children die,

19:32.004 --> 19:34.548
you keep them alive in your heart.

19:35.799 --> 19:37.217
You can't let them go.

19:37.718 --> 19:39.219
You keep them in here.

19:43.557 --> 19:45.309
So go ahead, just take the money.

19:46.310 --> 19:48.520
I'm giving it to my son
when I give it to you.

19:57.779 --> 19:59.198
I'll make you proud.

20:00.532 --> 20:02.659
I promise you I'll live a good life.

20:09.208 --> 20:10.292
We'll make you proud.

20:12.544 --> 20:14.087
That's all I could've wanted.

20:25.307 --> 20:30.729
A MIDSUMMER NIGHT'S FULL NETS

20:33.440 --> 20:35.984
Allow me
to introduce Captain Yang!

20:37.736 --> 20:40.364
I wish all your days
could be as wonderful as this one!

20:41.240 --> 20:42.282
That's my son.

20:43.408 --> 20:44.701
Captain Yang!

20:45.494 --> 20:47.246
Don't you just love the sound of it?

20:47.913 --> 20:49.414
I know I do. Wow!

20:53.627 --> 20:54.962
There we are.

20:55.045 --> 20:57.881
What a day.
It's the best day of my life.

21:22.739 --> 21:23.907
God of the seas,

21:24.449 --> 21:27.286
may this ship not follow the fish,

21:27.369 --> 21:29.329
but may the fish follow the ship.

21:30.330 --> 21:32.833
May its nets always come back full!

21:32.916 --> 21:35.168
May its nets
always come back full!

21:35.252 --> 21:38.297
-May its nets always come back full!
-Nice and full!

21:38.380 --> 21:39.506
Nice and full!

21:43.927 --> 21:45.095
To the gods.

21:46.221 --> 21:48.890
It's nice.
Just as long as it stays afloat.

21:48.974 --> 21:51.351
Oh, Captain Yang.
Here, give me a bowl of makgeolli.

21:51.435 --> 21:53.854
-Well, what are the odds it doesn't?
-Whoo!

21:53.937 --> 21:56.523
How can that woman
make such a fool of herself?

21:58.567 --> 22:00.193
Whoo! All right!

22:00.694 --> 22:02.654
Captain Yang!

22:02.738 --> 22:04.072
Captain Yang!

22:04.156 --> 22:06.199
Captain Yang!

22:06.283 --> 22:08.160
Captain Yang!

22:08.243 --> 22:10.412
When my son, Gwan-sik, was born,

22:11.705 --> 22:15.792
the fortune teller said she saw him
with two sheds full of food!

22:15.876 --> 22:18.962
Now look at him, Captain Yang!

22:22.382 --> 22:24.634
♪ Captain Yang, Captain Yang ♪

22:24.718 --> 22:26.928
♪ Captain Yang, Captain Yang ♪

22:27.012 --> 22:29.973
♪ Captain Yang ♪

22:30.057 --> 22:31.767
Oh yeah!

22:32.601 --> 22:34.186
What's with that face?

22:34.269 --> 22:36.355
Oh, please,
you know exactly what this is for.

22:36.438 --> 22:38.982
So Jong-gu turned up, eh?
And you're jealous.

22:39.066 --> 22:40.359
You're his grandmother.

22:41.401 --> 22:44.613
You tell my grandson,
if he ever shows his face again,

22:44.696 --> 22:46.656
I'll report that brat
to the police for stealing.

22:46.740 --> 22:49.659
Come on, Jong-gu is still
your eldest grandchild.

22:49.743 --> 22:52.245
He'll perform
the ancestral rites after you pass.

22:52.329 --> 22:54.956
-He'll restore our fortunes.
-Ae-sun will do that.

22:56.500 --> 22:59.711
-She's my eldest son's daughter.
-♪ Captain Yang, Captain Yang ♪

22:59.795 --> 23:02.089
Listen up, everyone.
I have something to say!

23:02.172 --> 23:04.591
After four generations of the Yang family,

23:04.674 --> 23:07.427
my eldest son is Jeju's newest captain!

23:07.511 --> 23:13.225
Let's hear it for the Yangs!

23:13.308 --> 23:14.142
Yeah!

23:14.226 --> 23:16.478
I think you meant
the eldest daughter of the Ohs.

23:17.854 --> 23:19.606
Because, after all,

23:19.689 --> 23:22.275
it was my grandmother who bought the boat.

23:22.359 --> 23:24.569
I think the two sheds
in Gwan-sik's fortune

23:24.653 --> 23:26.947
must have been about me after all.

23:29.533 --> 23:32.411
All right, you're the blessing.
I admit it.

23:33.412 --> 23:36.206
-And what a big pile of blessings she is!
-Oh, is that right?

23:36.289 --> 23:37.332
Then you know what to do.

23:37.416 --> 23:38.875
Carry that pile on your back.

23:39.709 --> 23:41.878
Weren't you just complaining
how you took her in

23:41.962 --> 23:44.297
without so much as a silver spoon?

23:44.381 --> 23:47.509
Perhaps this boat
will change your tune, eh?

23:48.552 --> 23:50.595
-Yes, it will.
-Ae-sun. Ae-sun.

23:50.679 --> 23:53.223
What an honorable daughter-in-law she is!

23:53.306 --> 23:55.642
The best daughter-in-law in the world!

23:58.186 --> 24:00.814
Who bought him that boat again? Who?

24:01.481 --> 24:02.899
-You!
-You did!

24:02.983 --> 24:04.401
You'd die for that girl?

24:04.484 --> 24:07.404
Look how happy she is, my daughter-in-law.

24:07.487 --> 24:08.572
Hey, Dad?

24:08.655 --> 24:09.531
Look.

24:10.657 --> 24:13.910
-Isn't she the funniest girl in the world?
-Everybody, sing it with me.

24:13.994 --> 24:18.081
Oh Ae-sun! Oh Ae-sun!
Oh Ae-sun! Oh Ae-sun!

24:18.165 --> 24:22.002
During that season,
they stood tall like forest trees.

24:23.170 --> 24:27.174
It was the beginning of a summer
they'd never forget.

24:30.802 --> 24:31.845
Is she okay?

24:31.928 --> 24:32.929
Mom, you're peeing.

24:34.097 --> 24:34.931
Oh no.

24:35.765 --> 24:36.850
It's way too early.

24:36.933 --> 24:37.893
Ae-sun.

24:38.977 --> 24:41.480
-Honey! Aah!
-Take her to the hospital!

24:42.272 --> 24:45.400
-The baby's coming. The baby's coming.
-Honey, please! It's coming!

24:50.030 --> 24:52.282
-What's wrong?
-Quick, hurry!

24:52.365 --> 24:54.534
-Take her! Quickly!
-Careful. Careful.

24:55.285 --> 24:56.328
-Easy now.
-Careful.

25:14.387 --> 25:16.848
You were just laughing a second ago!

25:16.932 --> 25:18.558
You were cracking up!

25:19.434 --> 25:22.229
What did you do at my age?
What did you do every day?

25:37.285 --> 25:39.037
Mmm!

25:40.205 --> 25:43.917
You know Gwan-sik made these?
He's practically an expert by now.

25:44.000 --> 25:46.461
The best jeon you ever had!

25:51.716 --> 25:54.094
You always wanted a silver spoon.

25:54.177 --> 25:55.804
Now you finally have one.

25:55.887 --> 25:58.390
You must be so glad. Hmm.

25:59.099 --> 26:03.770
What an honorable grandson,
making all this for the ancestors.

26:03.853 --> 26:06.565
I mean, really,
you couldn't ask for a better one.

26:08.650 --> 26:11.611
So you're really
not gonna come to the ritual?

26:11.695 --> 26:13.947
Mm. He told me "no."

26:14.030 --> 26:15.198
He told you no?

26:15.282 --> 26:16.491
I want to go,

26:17.117 --> 26:18.702
but what can I do?

26:19.578 --> 26:20.870
I can't disobey my husband.

26:21.454 --> 26:25.500
Even if I mention the idea of getting near
your house, he gets furious.

26:25.584 --> 26:27.002
Oh, he's so scary.

26:28.545 --> 26:33.008
My granddaughter-in-law is a cut above
my daughter-in-law, it would seem.

26:33.091 --> 26:34.968
It figures. Gye-ok is a rabbit, after all,

26:35.051 --> 26:37.304
whereas I'm a snake,
and you're a baby tiger.

26:37.387 --> 26:40.640
Oh, come on.
Will you stop calling me a rabbit already?

26:40.724 --> 26:42.642
I can't help when I was born.

26:42.726 --> 26:46.438
There should be years for other animals,
like raccoons, moles, boars.

26:46.938 --> 26:49.608
What? You gonna list animals all day?

26:53.028 --> 26:54.029
Oh!

26:54.613 --> 26:55.447
Daddy!

26:56.823 --> 26:57.657
Here we go.

26:58.658 --> 27:00.493
Hey, you, how was your day?

27:00.577 --> 27:01.453
Give this to Mom.

27:05.165 --> 27:06.666
Well? What do you want?

27:07.250 --> 27:08.918
That's how you greet your mother?

27:09.419 --> 27:13.048
Oh, dear. Why do you carry him
on your back like that?

27:13.131 --> 27:15.133
You'll wake up with back pains
the next day.

27:16.009 --> 27:19.137
Let's see. There's my little grandson.

27:19.220 --> 27:20.472
What'd you come here for?

27:20.972 --> 27:22.807
To bother my wife? Huh?

27:22.891 --> 27:24.934
Are you hanging around here
to make her uncomfortable?

27:25.810 --> 27:26.936
What about me?

27:27.520 --> 27:30.523
Me? Does anyone care if I'm uncomfortable?

27:30.607 --> 27:31.900
Your mom likes me now.

27:32.651 --> 27:35.362
I gave birth to a son.
I made you a captain.

27:35.445 --> 27:37.697
I gave her some silver spoons.

27:37.781 --> 27:40.533
I've even given her
everything she could possibly want.

27:40.617 --> 27:42.702
She couldn't hate me if she wanted to.

27:42.786 --> 27:44.954
That would be strange, wouldn't it?

27:45.038 --> 27:47.415
If she hated me now?

27:48.041 --> 27:49.250
No doubt about it.

27:49.334 --> 27:52.045
My granddaughter-in-law is a cut above
my daughter-in-law. Yup.

27:52.629 --> 27:55.507
I guess that means
my son is better than your son, huh?

28:02.222 --> 28:05.266
Did he have to give them
all our octopus?

28:06.434 --> 28:08.436
What are we supposed to feed the kids?

28:12.357 --> 28:15.694
Where are you off to, then?
Did you get a house of your own?

28:16.403 --> 28:17.237
Yes.

28:17.904 --> 28:18.822
That's right, sir.

28:19.948 --> 28:21.449
We're moving into our own home.

28:21.533 --> 28:22.742
All right.

28:23.535 --> 28:24.369
Go on.

28:25.120 --> 28:26.329
I just wanted to say…

28:26.413 --> 28:27.497
Go on!

28:27.580 --> 28:28.665
Get moving!

28:29.666 --> 28:31.126
Sir, we really, really…

28:31.209 --> 28:32.419
Will you stop talking?

28:32.502 --> 28:34.629
I don't need to hear the words to know.

28:37.173 --> 28:38.049
I just wanted to say--

28:38.133 --> 28:39.342
Crybaby woman!

28:40.135 --> 28:41.469
Pack your bags.

28:42.470 --> 28:43.847
Thank you, sir, for everything.

28:45.432 --> 28:47.517
Might as well wake up the children.

28:48.059 --> 28:50.270
This is too much to eat by ourselves.

28:50.353 --> 28:52.439
We have to cook some pork to celebrate.

28:52.522 --> 28:54.482
Why are we packing?

28:56.317 --> 28:58.486
We know
it's been tough on you here.

28:58.570 --> 29:00.739
It couldn't have been easy

29:00.822 --> 29:04.117
living in that tiny room for so long,
was it?

29:05.326 --> 29:07.620
A family should have its own house.

29:36.483 --> 29:39.986
You told me that when you were six,
you would come up here by yourself and…

29:42.113 --> 29:43.573
Every morning, you'd wake up

29:44.741 --> 29:46.159
and start climbing the hill.

29:53.792 --> 29:56.085
Mommy! Mommy!

29:57.504 --> 29:59.589
Mommy!

30:01.424 --> 30:02.634
Oh, my baby!

30:03.259 --> 30:04.969
Did you walk here all by yourself?

30:05.053 --> 30:07.555
-Yeah.
-Oh, you precious thing.

30:10.225 --> 30:13.186
Mommy! Mommy!

30:13.686 --> 30:14.604
Oh my.

30:14.687 --> 30:17.232
-Mommy! Hey!
-It's so hot. Come here.

30:17.315 --> 30:19.025
Come here, my darling, come here.

30:19.108 --> 30:20.318
It's so hot outside.

30:20.401 --> 30:21.361
Are you all right?

30:21.444 --> 30:23.238
Look here. I made this.

30:23.321 --> 30:24.656
Do you like it?

30:24.739 --> 30:27.325
Oh, look, it's nice,

30:27.408 --> 30:28.910
and on such a hot day.

30:28.993 --> 30:30.161
You did so good.

30:30.245 --> 30:32.622
You did so good, sweetheart.

30:32.705 --> 30:33.915
Hey, Mom!

30:35.041 --> 30:37.794
Hey, Mom, I got a perfect score!

30:37.877 --> 30:40.296
Oh, my goodness, honey! It's so cold!

30:40.380 --> 30:42.715
How did you climb the hill
in this weather?

30:44.759 --> 30:45.927
SPELLING TEST

30:46.010 --> 30:48.096
-A perfect score.
-A perfect score.

30:48.179 --> 30:49.430
Well done, honey.

30:49.514 --> 30:50.974
You did so well.

30:59.607 --> 31:01.651
You loved coming here to see your mom.

31:05.655 --> 31:07.448
You said whenever you came here,

31:08.199 --> 31:09.826
you could smell her cooking a mile away.

31:17.834 --> 31:20.169
You told me how your mother
dove for abalone every day

31:20.253 --> 31:21.713
so she could buy this house.

31:25.091 --> 31:26.467
We're not renting it?

31:28.720 --> 31:29.929
I saw it for sale.

31:30.013 --> 31:31.014
Now it's ours.

31:31.723 --> 31:33.433
The previous owner is in Busan.

31:34.142 --> 31:37.395
-It's hard for him to manage anyway.
-You mean, there's no lease?

31:39.856 --> 31:40.773
A home of our own.

31:46.946 --> 31:48.573
I never had a home before, not…

31:50.408 --> 31:51.910
not even once.

31:51.993 --> 31:55.288
Even the conches and crabs
have a place they call their own.

31:56.915 --> 31:58.124
But I never did.

31:59.626 --> 32:01.210
Not once in my whole life.

32:03.755 --> 32:05.048
My mom's house,

32:05.882 --> 32:07.383
my uncle's house,

32:08.343 --> 32:11.429
even my stepdad's house in Dodong-ri.
None of them…

32:12.597 --> 32:14.515
…none of them were my home.

32:16.017 --> 32:17.435
But this is actually…

32:18.102 --> 32:19.312
It really is…

32:20.229 --> 32:21.064
Honey,

32:22.565 --> 32:23.608
you like it?

32:23.691 --> 32:24.567
Mm-hmm.

32:25.109 --> 32:26.110
I do.

32:26.986 --> 32:27.987
So much.

32:29.072 --> 32:30.782
I'm so happy, Gwan-sik.

32:36.996 --> 32:37.830
Aw.

32:46.965 --> 32:50.009
Next time,
I'll buy us an even bigger house.

32:50.843 --> 32:53.680
But this already feels like a palace.

32:55.098 --> 32:56.265
And because it's mine,

32:58.184 --> 33:00.019
it's even better than a palace.

33:03.773 --> 33:05.566
Yes, it's a little low.

33:06.109 --> 33:08.569
Summer is the season of nurturing.

33:09.112 --> 33:13.950
My parents had so much fun going from
a one-bedroom apartment to a proper house

33:14.659 --> 33:17.203
that they didn't mind
expending a little sweat.

33:17.286 --> 33:20.415
Hold on.
I think we need another one there.

33:20.498 --> 33:22.250
Yeah, right there. Put another one.

33:23.668 --> 33:26.337
That's a wardrobe with mother-of-pearl.

33:26.421 --> 33:28.131
Mother-of-pearl from Tongyeong.

33:28.631 --> 33:32.051
It's not secondhand.
It's brand new, and it's all mine.

33:32.135 --> 33:36.931
Geum-myeong.
Do you want it when you get older? Do you?

33:37.015 --> 33:40.435
Yes or no? Huh?
Of course you want it, don't you?

33:42.103 --> 33:43.479
Should we put up a picture?

33:43.563 --> 33:46.774
I think it's tacky. Mm. Should we?

33:48.276 --> 33:49.861
Many years later,

33:49.944 --> 33:53.072
even after they moved
to that apartment with a built-in closet…

33:53.156 --> 33:53.990
Eun-myeong.

33:54.073 --> 33:57.368
…Mom and Dad could never let go
of that mother-of-pearl closet.

33:58.619 --> 33:59.746
Here we go.

33:59.829 --> 34:00.955
Okay.

34:04.584 --> 34:06.544
That shiny pearl wardrobe…

34:06.627 --> 34:07.879
Mama-ma!

34:07.962 --> 34:11.632
…would always remind them
of their bright summer days.

35:04.352 --> 35:06.646
The previous family
were renters, all right.

35:06.729 --> 35:09.232
No one takes care of a place
they don't own.

35:09.774 --> 35:13.236
At the very least, they could've
pulled their hair out of the drain.

35:15.196 --> 35:16.948
Were you busy or what, Mom?

35:18.157 --> 35:20.827
You've never shown up
in my dream before, so…

35:23.287 --> 35:25.790
Did you come because we bought this house?

35:26.958 --> 35:27.917
Are you happy?

35:28.793 --> 35:30.169
Are you proud of me?

35:31.462 --> 35:33.005
Your neighbor bought a truck already.

35:34.215 --> 35:35.049
What?

35:35.550 --> 35:38.177
Does he think making babies
is all a husband does?

35:38.928 --> 35:42.140
You're about to give birth,
and he leaves you to go catch squids.

35:43.266 --> 35:45.226
It's the squids that bought this house.

35:45.726 --> 35:47.687
He should've bought a car by now.

35:50.648 --> 35:53.442
That neighbor of yours
has a truck and a license.

35:53.526 --> 35:56.028
Did you just come
to talk about our neighbor?

35:56.112 --> 35:57.822
Are you that jealous of her truck?

35:58.406 --> 36:01.242
It was a big deal for us
to buy the house.

36:02.076 --> 36:04.078
Why do you care so much about cars?

36:04.162 --> 36:06.164
Don't let her take your persimmons.

36:06.914 --> 36:09.709
Some branches of your tree
reach over into her yard.

36:12.378 --> 36:13.880
Make sure she doesn't steal.

36:14.630 --> 36:17.091
Whatever she takes, she has to pay for.

36:20.428 --> 36:21.554
Ae-sun,

36:22.597 --> 36:23.431
just remember,

36:24.307 --> 36:25.474
she has a truck.

36:29.812 --> 36:31.189
She has a truck.

36:45.077 --> 36:45.912
Geum-myeong.

36:48.748 --> 36:49.916
Geum-myeong.

36:51.751 --> 36:54.837
Run next door
to the neighbor's house, okay?

37:27.453 --> 37:29.288
♪ La, da, di, da, da ♪

37:33.209 --> 37:36.963
Whether boys or girls,
let's have two kids and raise them well.

37:40.258 --> 37:45.263
You only had two children, Gye-ok.
Now Ae-sun here has three.

37:45.346 --> 37:49.141
The eldest girl, Geum-myeong,
brought them good fortune.

37:49.225 --> 37:51.978
Now she's been blessed
with two healthy sons.

37:52.061 --> 37:57.358
My granddaughter-in-law is a cut above
my daughter-in-law, indeed.

37:57.441 --> 37:59.235
She's a cut above everything!

38:00.194 --> 38:02.738
I thought you said
Ae-sun wasn't destined to have any boys.

38:02.822 --> 38:06.617
If an ancestor comes to you
in a dream before childbirth,

38:06.701 --> 38:08.244
the child will be a great blessing.

38:09.161 --> 38:12.415
Because of this boy,
Gwan-sik will have full nets.

38:12.498 --> 38:13.833
Mark my words.

38:13.916 --> 38:16.585
This child has been blessed
by his grandma.

38:16.669 --> 38:19.338
You used to say
her mother's ghost haunted her.

38:19.422 --> 38:20.965
Now she's an "ancestor"?

38:21.048 --> 38:22.466
I can see it now.

38:23.259 --> 38:26.554
This little one will do well in life,
setbacks and all.

38:27.305 --> 38:30.683
You said before Ae-sun was destined
for a life of misfortune.

38:30.766 --> 38:32.351
Maybe you're just a…

38:33.561 --> 38:34.562
A what?

38:35.187 --> 38:36.397
A charlatan?

38:36.480 --> 38:38.232
You could be more accurate.

38:41.527 --> 38:44.030
Full nets!

38:44.113 --> 38:45.406
Full nets!

38:45.489 --> 38:48.034
Gwan-sik's boat has full nets!

38:49.535 --> 38:51.162
That little boy is a blessing.

38:51.245 --> 38:53.372
Fish can't leave
your husband's boat alone.

38:53.456 --> 38:55.875
Uh-huh.
The real blessing around here is Ae-sun.

38:56.667 --> 38:59.920
As you can see,
I'm destined for marvelous things.

39:00.004 --> 39:01.964
Yes, you are!

39:03.174 --> 39:06.510
Our democracy has chosen
its representative for the people.

39:07.053 --> 39:09.597
All right, there's no one
against me, is there?

39:10.598 --> 39:13.184
So it's basically unanimous, isn't it?

39:13.851 --> 39:14.727
No need to vote.

39:14.810 --> 39:16.896
President Park Chung-hee,
as the sole candidate,

39:16.979 --> 39:20.483
received 2,577 ayes and one…

39:20.566 --> 39:23.110
You're the chief,
same as you always are.

39:24.695 --> 39:26.697
I nominate Oh Ae-sun for deputy chief.

39:26.781 --> 39:27.782
I second!

39:27.865 --> 39:28.741
I third!

39:28.824 --> 39:29.658
Let her do it!

39:29.742 --> 39:31.702
Aw, no way. I'd never.

39:31.786 --> 39:34.789
You know I'm not interested in politics.

39:34.872 --> 39:36.499
Who's Oh Ae-sun?

39:36.582 --> 39:39.377
-Gwang-rye's daughter.
-Oh, well, if she's Gwang-rye's daughter…

39:39.460 --> 39:40.836
Exactly!

39:40.920 --> 39:44.090
Let her stand for the position.
Let's vote.

39:44.173 --> 39:46.592
Back in school,
she was class vice president.

39:46.675 --> 39:48.135
-Make her deputy chief!
-That's right!

39:48.219 --> 39:51.180
Veto. I veto your request.

39:51.847 --> 39:54.725
The president gets to appoint
his cabinet members all by himself.

39:55.643 --> 39:58.896
You think Rhee Syngman and Chang Myon
were on the same level? Really?

39:58.979 --> 40:01.941
That's pretty tough talk
for someone who ran unopposed.

40:03.025 --> 40:05.903
Well, in any case,
it's campaign standard. Right?

40:05.986 --> 40:07.613
Basic standards are necessary

40:07.696 --> 40:09.990
so not everyone's
mom and their dog run for office.

40:10.074 --> 40:12.743
Excuse me, please,
it's one free cake per person.

40:12.827 --> 40:15.037
-But you have so many.
-I should run for chief instead.

40:15.121 --> 40:17.832
If a dog can run for office,
why can't someone's mom?

40:22.670 --> 40:23.671
W… what'd you say?

40:24.255 --> 40:26.841
Honestly, I never thought of running,

40:27.466 --> 40:29.218
but being someone's deputy,

40:29.301 --> 40:30.928
I don't think I could handle it.

40:31.679 --> 40:33.848
You said yourself
there wouldn't be a vote otherwise.

40:33.931 --> 40:36.267
I think people
should at least have a choice.

40:36.350 --> 40:37.184
That's right!

40:37.268 --> 40:38.727
-Yes!
-That's right, yes!

40:38.811 --> 40:40.896
What have I got to lose? All right.

40:41.397 --> 40:42.773
May the best candidate win.

40:43.357 --> 40:47.695
The girl challenging the village chief
is Gwang-rye's daughter!

40:47.778 --> 40:50.656
You're joking. A woman as village chief?

40:51.532 --> 40:53.659
What? Are you afraid?

40:55.661 --> 40:57.079
Afraid?

40:57.621 --> 40:58.456
Goodness.

40:59.290 --> 41:00.583
How dare you!

41:00.666 --> 41:02.543
If you're not afraid of it, let's vote.

41:02.626 --> 41:04.336
You? You'll run against me?

41:05.337 --> 41:06.422
Ooh.

41:07.298 --> 41:09.175
You wanna run against me, yup?

41:10.050 --> 41:10.968
You?

41:11.051 --> 41:12.219
W… w… what?

41:12.303 --> 41:15.055
I'd let her be deputy chief if I were you.

41:15.139 --> 41:17.266
Don't embarrass yourself
by losing the vote.

41:22.188 --> 41:25.191
I never knew Ae-sun was such a comedian!

41:33.491 --> 41:35.993
A SMALL BALL LAUNCHED BY AE-SUN

41:36.076 --> 41:38.245
Ae-sun gave it her best shot,

41:39.788 --> 41:43.083
and Dodong-ri had
its first female deputy chief.

41:43.584 --> 41:46.545
Hey, come on.
Stop talking and look straight ahead.

41:47.505 --> 41:48.714
Look this way.

41:48.797 --> 41:51.008
Tall people move to the back of the line.

41:51.091 --> 41:53.219
If you're shorter, come up front. Okay?

41:53.844 --> 41:56.138
Hey, come on. Squeeze in. Squeeze in.

41:56.222 --> 41:58.307
One, two.

41:58.390 --> 42:01.018
Hey! Count to three
and then take the picture.

42:01.101 --> 42:01.977
Are you stupid?

42:02.853 --> 42:05.272
All right.
Everyone, look here.

42:05.356 --> 42:07.191
One, two, three.

42:10.069 --> 42:11.195
SOCIAL DANCE CLASS

42:11.278 --> 42:14.740
Shut up. You're coming with me
straight out the front door!

42:14.823 --> 42:16.992
Stop talking and move it! Move!

42:21.372 --> 42:24.625
-I got 'em. Hurry up and take the picture!
-Here come the delinquents now.

42:24.708 --> 42:26.126
Look at 'em. Look at 'em!

42:26.210 --> 42:27.753
Take the picture. Stop talking!

42:27.836 --> 42:29.838
All right,
bring 'em here, right here.

42:30.756 --> 42:32.258
Shut your mouth and sit down.

42:32.341 --> 42:34.343
-Hurry!
-Gather them all like a pile of crap.

42:34.426 --> 42:36.762
-A runner!
-That's enough! You can settle down now.

42:36.845 --> 42:39.515
There's more down there.
We should check. Out of my way.

42:39.598 --> 42:40.849
Check inside.

42:41.725 --> 42:43.143
There has to be a few more.

42:45.020 --> 42:47.231
Hey, is someone in there? Move aside.

42:47.314 --> 42:49.233
Wait, hey!

42:49.316 --> 42:51.193
That's the ladies' room, you weirdo.

42:51.694 --> 42:54.989
You little brat.
How dare you call me a weirdo!

42:55.072 --> 42:56.907
The ladies' room is my jurisdiction.

42:59.159 --> 43:00.703
You have a crush on me or what?

43:00.786 --> 43:02.788
Why do you always show up everywhere I go?

43:03.330 --> 43:04.498
Just go away.

43:04.582 --> 43:06.584
Go live somewhere else on the island.

43:08.794 --> 43:11.171
What? You still think of me?

43:16.885 --> 43:18.012
Second thoughts?

43:28.564 --> 43:30.190
Hey, why'd you pinch your nose?

43:30.983 --> 43:32.359
Why'd you pinch your nose?

43:33.152 --> 43:34.737
I was talking to you, you brat!

43:40.618 --> 43:42.870
Come on out.

43:43.412 --> 43:44.747
It's all over now.

43:44.830 --> 43:47.249
You have been surrounded already.

43:50.252 --> 43:52.212
Is someone in there or not?

44:00.929 --> 44:01.764
Huh?

44:03.891 --> 44:05.142
Those feet…

44:08.187 --> 44:10.147
The hell with ballroom dancing.

44:10.230 --> 44:13.150
We never needed dancing
to mingle back in my day.

44:13.233 --> 44:14.985
Ever since the New Community Movement,

44:15.069 --> 44:17.655
you people have gotten
way too comfortable.

44:17.738 --> 44:19.865
You think life is one big party every day?

44:20.407 --> 44:22.785
No one would've done this in the war.

44:22.868 --> 44:25.120
Send these go-go dancers
to the Northern border.

44:26.413 --> 44:29.291
You're supposed to count to three.
I already told you so!

44:38.842 --> 44:41.011
I don't believe it.

44:45.182 --> 44:46.517
You're kidding!

44:46.600 --> 44:49.520
What are you doing here?
What are we supposed to do?

44:51.897 --> 44:53.774
What are we supposed to do now?

44:56.610 --> 44:59.029
Fine. This is crazy.

45:05.661 --> 45:07.538
Oh, how do we get you out of here?

45:08.414 --> 45:09.665
Okay, out the window.

45:16.004 --> 45:18.841
Hey, at least cover your faces.

45:18.924 --> 45:20.801
Quick, cover up your daughter's face.

45:23.804 --> 45:24.847
Good idea.

45:24.930 --> 45:26.974
Look at these well-fed women.

45:27.057 --> 45:29.518
They have nothing to do,
so they just go out dancing.

45:29.601 --> 45:30.978
I can't believe this.

45:31.061 --> 45:34.231
You will never face reality
until you're forced to struggle.

45:34.314 --> 45:36.525
You have it too easy. Yeah.

45:36.608 --> 45:38.277
Your lives are just too good.

45:38.360 --> 45:40.279
Dancing will be a real sport someday.

45:41.697 --> 45:43.991
Nice. Real sport, my foot.

45:44.575 --> 45:47.786
If it's a real sport,
why are you covering your faces?

45:47.870 --> 45:51.248
Why don't you show your face
and go to the Olympics? Dancing will be…

45:51.331 --> 45:52.374
Hyeon-suk, wait.

45:52.958 --> 45:55.335
One, two, three!

45:55.961 --> 45:58.130
-One, two, three.
-Dancing will never be a sport.

45:58.630 --> 46:00.299
All right, enough pictures.

46:07.765 --> 46:10.350
-Oh no.
-That woman is fleeing with her child! Ha!

46:10.434 --> 46:11.977
They're like refugees from the war.

46:12.936 --> 46:15.189
Get a picture of her.
Get a picture of that woman!

46:15.272 --> 46:17.357
Get a picture of her!

46:17.441 --> 46:20.360
Don't worry! I'll go get them!

46:25.991 --> 46:27.326
Stop right there!

46:29.203 --> 46:32.206
What the hell?
This was supposed to be my thing.

46:34.291 --> 46:36.168
At least Ae-sun is doing something.

46:38.086 --> 46:40.172
You just tell the photographer
to take a picture,

46:40.255 --> 46:41.673
say cheese, and that's it.

46:52.142 --> 46:53.811
They're going to put you
on the news tonight

46:53.894 --> 46:56.104
for going dancing
with your child for sure.

46:56.188 --> 46:58.148
Are you doing this because you're bored?

46:58.232 --> 47:00.651
Do you have too much money to spend?

47:00.734 --> 47:04.696
If I didn't get to dance
the jitterbug sometimes, I'd go crazy.

47:05.197 --> 47:07.825
I would've killed myself or someone else.

47:11.036 --> 47:13.789
At home, I feel a rage
from deep within myself, Ae-sun.

47:15.707 --> 47:17.084
But when I start dancing,

47:17.167 --> 47:18.585
it all goes away.

47:19.461 --> 47:20.838
So I can't help it.

47:20.921 --> 47:22.130
I keep on dancing.

47:25.759 --> 47:28.971
So your husband, does he still--

47:29.054 --> 47:31.014
He's the same asshole he's always been.

47:31.598 --> 47:33.809
He practically nicknamed me
"How dare you!"

47:33.892 --> 47:35.269
How dare you!

47:36.144 --> 47:39.231
Every day, it's,
"How dare you! How dare you!"

47:39.314 --> 47:42.109
Hyeon-suk learned to say
"How dare you" before "Da-da."

47:42.901 --> 47:44.695
Hey, Mommy, you are Cinderella.

47:46.321 --> 47:47.322
Huh?

47:48.156 --> 47:48.991
You're right.

47:49.074 --> 47:53.328
Well, Cinderella's slipper fell off
because she danced before she ran away.

48:00.460 --> 48:02.504
That makes your dad a prince.

48:09.428 --> 48:10.846
These might work better.

48:10.929 --> 48:13.765
You have to wear something similar
if you don't want them to suspect you.

48:14.516 --> 48:16.226
And who knows?

48:16.727 --> 48:19.146
One of these days, the prince of Dodong-ri

48:19.730 --> 48:21.690
will return your glass slipper.

48:22.274 --> 48:24.192
Tell me. That hairpin.

48:24.276 --> 48:26.486
Did your husband really buy it for you?

48:26.987 --> 48:28.405
That's what everyone says.

48:29.489 --> 48:32.576
They say your husband
spends his money buying you hairpins.

48:34.578 --> 48:35.537
Oh, really?

48:36.246 --> 48:39.917
Uh, this village worries
far too much about my hairpins.

48:42.127 --> 48:44.087
But you have changed, Ae-sun.

48:44.671 --> 48:45.881
They all see it.

48:46.715 --> 48:48.759
You dress better than you did before.

48:49.468 --> 48:51.136
Like you're high-class.

48:53.680 --> 48:55.349
How people dress tends to

48:56.683 --> 48:58.602
reflect how they live.

49:06.401 --> 49:07.611
How dare…

49:10.322 --> 49:12.824
Well, if you're so unhappy,
you should leave him.

49:12.908 --> 49:14.743
It's not like he's some great man.

49:14.826 --> 49:16.620
You shouldn't let him crush you.

49:18.622 --> 49:20.123
Is that why you turned him down?

49:20.749 --> 49:21.583
Huh?

49:22.209 --> 49:23.168
You really don't

49:24.044 --> 49:25.504
have second thoughts?

49:27.923 --> 49:31.593
You have a crush on me or what?
Why do you always show up everywhere I go?

49:32.302 --> 49:33.553
Just go away.

49:34.304 --> 49:35.847
Go live somewhere else on the island.

49:38.392 --> 49:39.226
What?

49:40.185 --> 49:41.353
You still think of me?

49:43.063 --> 49:44.022
Second thoughts?

49:46.441 --> 49:48.110
-Goodbye.
-Thank you.

49:48.860 --> 49:52.072
I have ears, you know.
I heard about everything.

49:52.572 --> 49:56.243
I found out you and my husband
were involved in the past.

49:58.704 --> 50:01.039
What? Is that… is that what they said?

50:01.123 --> 50:03.000
Nothing happened. I swear.

50:03.083 --> 50:06.044
We just… We went on one blind date.

50:06.128 --> 50:08.088
Just once when I was younger back then.

50:09.923 --> 50:11.425
Why did you leave it there?

50:12.050 --> 50:13.927
You should've taken him for yourself.

50:14.970 --> 50:17.848
Then you would've landed
in this pile of crap instead.

50:23.145 --> 50:26.189
Hyeon-suk, never step on a pile of poop.

50:26.273 --> 50:30.694
Instead, you should marry a man
like this lady's husband, okay?

50:42.414 --> 50:44.833
Airplane!

51:16.198 --> 51:18.533
Your handwriting
is much better than mine.

51:20.911 --> 51:22.621
Shouldn't the bookworm do the writing?

51:34.800 --> 51:36.009
Should I get on the boat?

51:36.927 --> 51:38.053
The paint will dry fast.

51:39.721 --> 51:42.057
It's bad luck for women
to get on the boat.

51:42.140 --> 51:45.310
They say the Dragon King will sink it,
and you won't be able to return again.

51:45.393 --> 51:47.395
I don't believe in that.

51:47.479 --> 51:49.022
Stop it, Gwan-sik.

51:49.106 --> 51:51.942
The Dragon King is vengeful.
All the gods are.

51:52.025 --> 51:53.485
Well, I don't believe in any of them.

51:54.277 --> 51:57.572
You, Geum-myeong, Eun-myeong,
Dong-myeong are my gods.

51:57.656 --> 51:59.908
Even in a typhoon,
I'll make it back because of you.

51:59.991 --> 52:01.368
I'll never die.

52:01.952 --> 52:03.370
I'll always come back.

52:06.164 --> 52:07.249
I'll always come back home.

52:12.379 --> 52:15.257
I know you will.
You're my Steelheart after all.

52:17.425 --> 52:18.426
So get in.

52:19.427 --> 52:20.679
You're my blessing, right?

52:20.762 --> 52:24.099
So I need you to write it
to keep our fortunes strong.

52:37.320 --> 52:38.697
Mom always said,

52:38.780 --> 52:40.991
"It's bad luck
if a girl gets on the boat."

52:42.159 --> 52:45.370
But in that moment,
she didn't have the heart to tell me.

52:49.374 --> 52:52.586
She didn't want her daughter
to inherit that kind of world,

52:52.669 --> 52:54.921
so Mom did what she had to.

52:55.005 --> 52:56.923
She challenged the superstition.

53:42.510 --> 53:44.971
I never really believed
in the Dragon King anyway

53:45.055 --> 53:46.556
'cause I believe in myself!

53:47.265 --> 53:50.018
Why should it be bad luck for me
or Geum-myeong to get on the boat?

53:51.019 --> 53:55.148
What? Haven't you heard what's been
going on up here, you stupid old man?

53:56.274 --> 53:58.818
You ever heard about
the New Community Movement?

53:59.486 --> 54:01.738
I thought you said
all the gods were vengeful.

54:01.821 --> 54:04.241
Eun-myeong, Dong-myeong, come here.

54:04.324 --> 54:05.909
Well, I'm vengeful too.

54:05.992 --> 54:09.663
What about the Anti-shamanism Movement?
Heard of that one, have you?

54:10.247 --> 54:14.209
These days, the president himself
arrests people who do rituals for you.

54:15.377 --> 54:16.795
So be nice to me, or else…

54:16.878 --> 54:20.423
or else I won't serve you a bowl
of dried rice during the festivals.

54:21.466 --> 54:23.802
You just eat whatever I cook,
and you're gonna like it.

54:23.885 --> 54:26.054
As if I can't stand in my own boat?

54:26.137 --> 54:28.515
Take that, you weird old man!

54:29.683 --> 54:30.558
Spit at him.

54:35.897 --> 54:38.483
It was
the nurturing season of summer,

54:38.566 --> 54:40.860
and my young parents were growing up.

55:08.096 --> 55:09.597
GEUMEUNDONG

55:21.151 --> 55:21.985
Well,

55:23.194 --> 55:24.529
we have a house

55:25.447 --> 55:26.823
and even a boat.

55:28.033 --> 55:29.492
This is insane.

55:31.411 --> 55:32.329
You happy?

55:33.246 --> 55:34.080
Mm-hmm.

55:35.373 --> 55:36.416
Yeah.

55:38.501 --> 55:40.170
I am, Gwan-sik.

55:49.804 --> 55:51.931
-With the world in their hands…
-Stop.

55:53.016 --> 55:55.352
…the only thing they wanted now

55:55.852 --> 55:58.021
was for their summer to last.

56:00.565 --> 56:01.941
They had no idea

56:02.859 --> 56:04.611
what else summer could bring.

56:08.490 --> 56:09.866
FULL NETS

56:09.949 --> 56:14.496
A MIDSUMMER NIGHT'S FULL NETS

58:59.786 --> 59:04.624
"IN THE HOPE THAT OUR ECHOES
WILL FLOW AND FLOW UNTIL THEY REACH YOU."
